// The art book's frame for the entry round (doc/workflows/art_book.md, step 0): written once for the game, composed around each brief's entry.
pitch = "A page of a game's art direction book. The game: a factory builder on planets, from the surface down into the caves and up to orbit: mining, refining, automation and logistics. Stylised realism: real light on real materials, simplified shapes, low texture detail, no outlines, no cartoon palette. Machines are compact and squat, packed into their box, one big readable feature each, painted panels chipped at the edges to the metal, grime in the seams, moss taking hold where it is cool and damp, lit by what glows."
page = "Paint the machine into the attached empty page of the book, keeping its paper, its layout, its drawing style and its astronaut: fill the hero frame with one large three quarter view of the machine in its setting beside the astronaut, fill the front and side elevation boxes with sketches with the envelope dimensioned, add callouts naming each major part, fill the four swatches with its palette colours and name them, and write the machine's name in the title band; the only lettering is the title, the callouts, the dimensions and the swatch names."
